{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01JrqRA2n6wojsG6A3qNf3XQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`cards_drawn_this_turn` is set in `draw_card()` but never reset. So it accumulates across turns. I need to reset it at the start of each turn (during UNTAP step or at the beginning of a new turn).\n\nActually, looking at this, I should NOT modify the engine to reset `cards_drawn_this_turn` per turn - that would be an engine change for this card. Instead I'll track the \"first draw this turn\" on the card itself by listening to the `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` and comparing to when the last draw happened (using `turn_number`).\n\nIn the `register_triggers`, I'll track `_last_miracle_turn` on each card. When `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` fires:\n- Check if the drawn card is an instant or sorcery in the controller's hand\n- Check if this is the first draw of the current turn by comparing the current `game.turn_number` to the last turn we saw a draw\n- If both conditions are met, offer to cast for the miracle cost\n\nSince `cards_drawn_this_turn` doesn't reset between turns, I'll use the turn number itself to determine if we're in a new turn and this is the first draw.\n\nI can store a dictionary on the card object mapping player indices to the turn number when they last drew, then check if the current turn is different from the stored one to identify the first draw of each turn.\n\nFor the miracle mechanic itself, I need to implement a trigger that fires when a card is drawn—if it has miracle and it's the first draw this turn, the player gets an option to cast it for the reduced cost of two mana.\n\nThe trigger checks three things: whether Lorehold is on the battlefield and controlled by the right player, whether the drawn card is an instant or sorcery in hand, and whether this is the first draw of the turn using the tracker. If all conditions are met, I offer the player the choice to cast it.\n\nNow I'm looking at how to actually cast the spell with the overridden cost—`cast_spell_free` ignores costs entirely, so I need to find a way to cast it with a specific mana cost instead.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":307,"cache_read_input_tokens":57503,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":307},"output_tokens":23,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8a32b7f0-be82-4ad8-afb4-a624c81177bb","uuid":"63d32afa-b3b0-42b6-9583-9349dea9ffa1","request_id":"req_011CbwLF9r727KGfWYw1vvWt"}
