{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01E52r3EuBcN5HJHRuiLYYMt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see that `cast_spell_free` doesn't require mana payment. For Miracle, the player should pay {2} (not cast for free). So I need a different approach for Miracle casting.\n\nOptions:\n1. Use `cast_spell` but temporarily override the mana cost to {2}\n2. Add mana manually and use the normal cast flow\n3. Check if the player has {2} available and deduct it manually\n\nThe simplest approach: temporarily override `mana_cost` to `ManaCost(generic=2)`, move the card from hand to stack, pay {2}, then restore. \n\nBut modifying the full cast pipeline gets complicated. Looking at Miracle more carefully, I need to check if the player can pay the miracle cost, offer them the choice, and if they accept, move the card to the stack and deduct the mana. The cleanest way is probably to handle this during the draw trigger's resolution when the player decides whether to miracle cast. Writing the miracle trigger handler... Writing miracle casting logic... the card to the stack directly and pay the mana manually, bypassing the normal casting restrictions. This is simpler than trying to work around the timing checks, and I can look at how other special casting scenarios are implemented in the codebase for reference.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":826,"cache_read_input_tokens":58812,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":826},"output_tokens":31,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8a32b7f0-be82-4ad8-afb4-a624c81177bb","uuid":"c58d3f4e-92fc-4dba-925d-c604d194fb6e","request_id":"req_011CbwLH6sKb3iidXHgPfYYR"}
