{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_019FzTXdN9yJQiJYZHrrHGHg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the pattern. For the Miracle mechanic, I need to implement a `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` listener that:\n1. Checks the controller drew the card (event.player is ctrl)\n2. The card is an instant or sorcery\n3. It's the first draw this turn\n4. Lorehold is on the battlefield\n5. Offers player to cast for {2}\n\nFor \"first draw this turn\" check, I'll use a tracker dict on the Lorehold card keyed by player id → last turn number of first draw offer. \n\nFor the actual miracle casting: since we need to cast with alternate cost {2}, and we're in a trigger resolution context (not priority), I'll:\n- Temporarily override the card's mana cost to {2}\n- Move the card from hand to stack, bypassing the normal timing restrictions that would prevent casting during trigger resolution\n- Let the rest of the casting pipeline handle target selection and mana payment with the reduced cost\n\nNow I need to see how StackObject gets created and pushed to understand where to inject this logic.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3243,"cache_read_input_tokens":59638,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3243},"output_tokens":26,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8a32b7f0-be82-4ad8-afb4-a624c81177bb","uuid":"a324fae8-fc49-41e4-b72e-21e1fb1d24dc","request_id":"req_011CbwLKTsBsUGSLypxyV3Ej"}
