{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01TFMVefeouwKYS476Xr8Xqx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The test `test_miracle_not_offered_for_creature` is failing because the stack is not empty after drawing the creature. Let me think about what's on the stack...\n\nThe `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` fires and puts a trigger effect on the stack. Even if the condition is True (the player drew a card), the trigger goes onto the stack and then resolves. During resolution, it checks if the card is instant/sorcery and returns without doing anything. So the stack should have been empty after... wait, actually the trigger goes on the stack and then needs to be resolved.\nActually, I see the issue now. When the `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` fires, the trigger condition evaluates to True since the player is the controller, so the trigger gets queued onto the stack. The test checks if the stack is empty immediately after drawing, but the trigger is still sitting there waiting to resolve. I need to either call the stack resolution method before checking, or reconsider what the test should be asserting.\n\nThe `_draw_effect` function only does something if the drawn card is an instant or sorcery, otherwise it returns early. So the fix is to resolve the trigger from the stack first, then verify the stack is empty afterward and the creature remains in hand.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":786,"cache_read_input_tokens":73678,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":786},"output_tokens":40,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8a32b7f0-be82-4ad8-afb4-a624c81177bb","uuid":"b408c715-1aa2-4c2c-bc26-156c8566eb75","request_id":"req_011CbwLVrLpEWHwgFHBjyh7V"}
